  "steps": [
    { "text": "Warm a little {{oil}} in a deep skillet over medium heat. Add the {{onion}} and {{garlic}} and fry until softened.", "timer": { "minutes": 5, "label": "Soften onion & garlic" } },
    { "text": "Add the {{chorizo}} and fry until it releases its oil. For a richer sauce, stir in a tablespoon of tomato paste here.", "timer": { "minutes": 5, "label": "Fry the chorizo" } },
    { "text": "Stir in the {{paprika}} and {{oregano}}, then add about 500ml of the {{stock}} and the {{pasta}} \u2014 just enough to cover it. Lid on and simmer until nearly al dente, stirring now and then and topping up with stock if it starts to stick.", "timer": { "minutes": 8, "label": "Simmer the pasta" } },
    { "text": "Lid off. Pour in the {{cream}} and {{balsamic}}, season with salt and pepper, and stir. Simmer to thicken the sauce and finish cooking the pasta.", "timer": { "minutes": 2, "label": "Thicken the sauce" } },
    { "text": "When it's as saucy as you like and the pasta is al dente, divide between bowls and top with grated {{parmesan}} and {{chives}}." }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Use good Spanish cooking chorizo (the firm, cured kind) and cube it yourself rather than buying thin slices.",
    "Roughly 100g of dried pasta per person is a good portion guide.",
    "Leftovers keep 2\u20133 days in the fridge; reheat gently with a splash of milk or water to loosen the sauce."
